# Unit {{.UnitID}}: {{.Title}}

Goal: implement unit {{.UnitID}} (plan section "{{.Section}}") of project
{{.Project}}, as a commit on top of the pinned base {{.Ref}}.

Inputs:
- `{{.UnitPath}}` is this unit's section of the plan, byte for byte. It is the
  brief: its scope, contract and acceptance criteria are authoritative.
- `{{.PlanPath}}` is the whole plan, for context only. Do not implement any
  other unit.
{{range .ExtraInputs}}- `{{.}}` is supporting material the plan bundles with every unit.
{{end}}
Before editing, check that `git rev-parse HEAD` prints {{.Ref}}; the workspace
is pinned to it, and the pin is also recorded at `.t3/base-commit`. If it does
not, stop and say so in `{{.Reports.Handoff}}`.

Scope: the change unit {{.UnitID}} asks for and nothing else. No push, tag,
release or deployment, and no nested campaign, task or review submission.

Outputs:
- The commit, declared as `{{.CommitName}}`: commit the change and its tests.
  HEAD when you finish is what the reviewer receives.
- `{{.Reports.Continuation}}`: goal, checklist, current step, blockers and the last
  verification, kept current as you work.
- `{{.Reports.Handoff}}`: base {{.Ref}}, resulting head, changed paths, design decisions
  and why, verification commands with their exit codes, limitations and open
  risks.
- `{{.Reports.Verification}}`: your fresh command log for this final HEAD.

While iterating, run the tests of the packages you changed and of their
importers rather than the whole suite. In a repository with a `test-affected`
make target, such as t3-steward, that is `make test-affected BASE={{.Ref}}`;
otherwise run focused checks of the changed packages and their importers
through the shell. This does not replace the verification below, which
still runs once.

Verification: {{if .Verify}}these commands run in the workspace after you stop, and every
one must exit 0:
{{range .Verify}}- `{{.}}`
{{end}}{{else}}the plan declares no verification commands. Run the checks the
brief names and record them, with their exit codes, in `{{.Reports.Handoff}}`.
{{end}}
Review: a separate review task reads the commit and `{{.Reports.Handoff}}` next. Do not
claim acceptance.

Acceptance criteria: the ones in `{{.UnitPath}}`.
{{if .AcceptanceTests}}
Write the named tests first and run them for initial failure where behavior is new.
Explain cases that cannot fail first, then implement. In `{{.Reports.Handoff}}`, map every case
to its test function and result.
{{end}}
Before any report or source write, rerun the current collision guard below, even when
preflight reused a cached receipt: that receipt is baseline evidence, not the current index.
Stop on failure; never follow links, delete existing bytes or repair collisions automatically.
```sh
{{.ReportCheck}}
